    "title": "Three more players added to Houston Cougars' availability report ahead of Colorado game - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Joseph Duarte ,\n2 hours ago UH defensive lineman Eddie Walls II was listed as probable after not being on Tuesday's initial availability report. (Jason Fochtman/Houston Chronicle) Three new players were added to the University of Houston 's second availability report released Wednesday night.\nOffensive linemen Jason Brooks Jr. and David Ndukwe , who both missed the Week 2 game against Rice , were listed as probable for Friday's Big 12 opener against Colorado.\nDefensive lineman Eddie Walls II was listed as probable after not being on Tuesday's first report.\nRunning back JayShon Ridgle was listed as questionable.\nSign up for Cougar Confidential\nYou'll get get in-depth news and analysis about UH’s basketball and football teams from reporter Joseph Duarte by signing up for the Cougar Confidential newsletter .\nLinebacker Cavan Tuley is no longer on the report after being listed as probable.\nUH players listed as out for Friday's Big 12 opener against Colorado:\nRe'Shaun Sanford, running back\nJ'Marion Burnette, running back\nAnthony Gangi Jr., wide receiver\nSamuel Padgitt, wide receiver\nQuindario Lee, defensive line\nUH players listed as questionable:\nJD Rhym, defensive back\nMarquis Shoulders, wide receiver\nJayShon Ridgle, running back\nUH players listed as probable:\nDevan Williams, wide receiver\nJason Brooks Jr., left guard\nDavid Ndukwe, left tackle\nDalton Merryman, right tackle\nEddie Walls II, defensive line\nSign up for Houston Chronicle newsletters here\nRead the original article on houstonchronicle.com",
